.TH ARCHIVE-ATLAS 1 "2026-10-18" "archive-atlas 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
archive-atlas \- index an APT archive and answer dependency questions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B archive-atlas
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B archive-atlas
parses the
.I Packages
files of an APT archive tree into a normalised SQLite database, then answers
dependency questions about that database.
.PP
Analysis is scoped to one series and one architecture, because that is the set
apt resolves against: dependencies do not cross series, and an amd64 package
cannot satisfy an arm64 dependency.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B index \fIarchive\fR \-o \fIdatabase\fR
Parse every
.I Packages
file under
.IR archive /dists .
Reads plain, gzip and xz files.  Refuses to overwrite an existing database
unless
.B \-\-force
is given.  Limit the series with
.BR \-\-series .
.TP
.B stats \fIdatabase\fR
Package counts and sizes by series, component and section.
.TP
.B broken \fIdatabase\fR
Dependencies that nothing in the same series and architecture satisfies,
with the reason split into "no package provides" and "version constraint not
satisfied".  Exits 1 when findings exist.
.TP
.B impact \fIdatabase\fR \fIname\fR
The reverse-dependency closure of
.IR name :
every package that would lose a dependency if it were removed.
.TP
.B cycles \fIdatabase\fR
Strongly connected components of the dependency graph.  Exits 1 when findings
exist.
.TP
.B duplicates \fIdatabase\fR
Names with more than one version, or present in more than one component.
.TP
.B orphans \fIdatabase\fR
Packages with no reverse dependency, excluding Essential packages and those
with required or important priority.
.TP
.B demo \fIdirectory\fR
Write a synthetic archive containing five known defects.  Useful for
evaluating the tool without downloading a mirror.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-series \fISERIES\fR
Restrict to one series.
.TP
.B \-\-arch \fIARCH\fR
Restrict to one architecture.
.TP
.B \-\-format text|json
Output format.  JSON is stable.
.TP
.B \-\-limit \fIN\fR
Maximum rows printed by
.B orphans
(default 20; JSON reports the full count separately).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No findings, or a command that does not report findings completed.
.TP
.B 1
Findings were reported by
.BR broken ,
.B duplicates
or
.BR cycles .
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, unreadable archive, or missing database.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I dists/<series>/<component>/binary-<arch>/Packages
The input.  Compressed variants are read directly.
.SH NOTES
Version comparison implements Debian Policy §5.6.12 and is verified against
.BR dpkg (1)
on generated version pairs.
.PP
Virtual packages count as dependencies: a package whose
.I Provides
satisfies a dependency is not an orphan.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt-cache (8),
.BR dpkg (1),
.BR dose-debcheck (1)
.PP
Debian Policy Manual §5.6.12 and §7.1.
